WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:02.540
Ah!

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.370
Eliezer?

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.137
Yes.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.672
It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.973
Welcome, welcome.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.320
This is beautiful!

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.440
Yes!

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.680
This is where the
Templars actually hung out?

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.240
In here?

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.078
No, no, no.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.680
This is not the Templar.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.180
We are in the right place,
but in the wrong time.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.480
Let's go.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.060
If we want to see
the Templar building,

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.292
we have to go down
beneath this church.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.800
[music playing]

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.060
Here?
This is it?

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.480
Yeah.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.007
Under this door, we are
going to see another world.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.242
We [inaudible].

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.076
This is like out
of a movie right now.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.277
Are you kidding me?

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.178
We're going to go
into a secret door--

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.012
Yeah.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.046
--behind a junk shop?

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.520
[key turning]

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.540
Wow.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.520
Let's go.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.680
What!

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.991
Wow!

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.559
This is incredible!

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.996
Now we are in the right
time, in the right place.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:06.199
Here we are in the
12th and 13th century.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.700
This is underground,
buried crypt.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.840
This is really where the
Templar was 800 years ago.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.880
So creepy.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:27.086
I'm standing in a room that
ancient, medieval knights, the

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.456
Knights Templar hung out in?

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:33.259
Yes, they lived here
more than 200 years.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.761
I bet they never
thought there'd be

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.162
a bionic foot on their floor.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.867
This is the first
floor of the building.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:45.638
But in the 13th century, the
crusader church was above us.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.842
So we were just standing,
a few moments ago, in

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.176
another church right above me?

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.311
Mm-hmm.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.046
So there's church upon church?

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.514
Yeah.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.583
It's kind of crazy because
when you stand down here,

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.818
it doesn't look all that
different from the church

00:01:58.885 --> 00:01:59.953
upstairs in terms of style.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.920
Because you have the arches--

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.021
The arches and
everything, yes.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.057
But if you are
looking carefully,

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:07.894
the Templar masonry
work, it's completely

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.129
another architecture.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.631
Wow.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:15.134
The stones are much bigger
than the 19th century building.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.638
Look at that.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.708
It's very famous in
the crusader period

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:25.712
that a lot of stones
has the masonry marks.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.513
Whoa.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.680
So you see you this line--

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:28.481
Or maybe here, this one.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.316
Oh, yes, exactly this one.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.219
So this is actually the
mark of somebody's chisel?

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:36.756
Mm-hmm, form of the Templar.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.492
Ah, this is so cool!

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:43.096
When you find something that
you can connect to the people

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.899
that actually built
this building,

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.568
this is what's so
exciting for me.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.270
Because you actually
get to the person?

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.104
Yes, exactly.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.773
[music playing]

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.608
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
Further below the modern city,

00:02:55.675 --> 00:03:01.080
about 10 feet beneath the
crypt, are more vaults.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:05.785
The secret chambers, a
medieval knights' crypt.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.088
Nuts.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.026
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
We've established

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.894
that this was a
Templar building,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.763
but I don't know
what it was used for.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:20.667
Wow!

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.374
(QUIETLY) Wow.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.810
This is carved out
of the earth, huh?

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.611
(ECHOING) Hello!

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.483
What is this?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.019
This is for
collecting rainwater.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:43.756
It's a huge,
underground water tank.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.391
You can actually
see the little channel

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:49.929
where the water pours in
from the rain, right there.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.698
The Holy Land is
very, very warm.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:55.234
We are in the Middle East
and you need the water.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.636
ALBERT LIN (VOICEOVER):
Eliezer has

00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:02.241
excavated three of these
25,000 gallon tanks so far.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.410
And he believes
there are many more.

